import{_ as s,o as a,c as i,a2 as t}from"./chunks/framework.DncwoWA8.js";const k=JSON.parse('{"title":"Install the skills you choose","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"guide/install.md","filePath":"guide/install.md"}'),n={name:"guide/install.md"};function l(o,e,r,p,h,d){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[t(`<h1 id="install-the-skills-you-choose" tabindex="-1">Install the skills you choose <a class="header-anchor" href="#install-the-skills-you-choose" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Install the skills you choose&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Each <a href="/projects/ai-skills/skills/">skill profile</a> has a command that selects only that skill. You do not need to install the whole collection or use the personal manager.</p><h2 id="before-you-start" tabindex="-1">Before you start <a class="header-anchor" href="#before-you-start" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Before you start&quot;">​</a></h2><p>All commands on this page need a working agent harness, Node.js 22.20 or newer, Git, and npm/npx. For the optional manager route below, the target project must also have at least one Git commit and worktree support. The catalogued workspace helper needs Bun before managed project writes.</p><p>Installation downloads code and changes personal or project files. Review the source, destinations, and applicable approvals first. No credentials are required to inspect the public collection. Custom harness configuration directories need their own reviewed setup.</p><h2 id="install-one-skill" tabindex="-1">Install one skill <a class="header-anchor" href="#install-one-skill" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Install one skill&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Review the target project&#39;s instructions and the skill source first. Run the selected profile&#39;s command from the target project. For example, this command selects only <code>asd-ste100-technical</code>:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">npx</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -y</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> skills@1.7.4</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> add</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> dragoscirjan/ai</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --skill</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> asd-ste100-technical</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The installer should report <code>asd-ste100-technical</code> as the selected skill. Follow its harness prompts and verify discovery in your chosen harness. Other profiles provide their own command, including pinned external sources where applicable.</p><p>Check the profile&#39;s required instruction packages separately. Direct Skills CLI installation does not install those requirements automatically. Optional companions remain optional.</p><h2 id="optional-reviewed-selection-manager" tabindex="-1">Optional reviewed selection manager <a class="header-anchor" href="#optional-reviewed-selection-manager" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Optional reviewed selection manager&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Use <code>sync-my-skills</code> only if you want it to inspect a project and propose a reviewed selection. Installing one skill does not require this route.</p><h3 id="_1-install-the-personal-manager" tabindex="-1">1. Install the personal manager <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-install-the-personal-manager" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1. Install the personal manager&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The following example selects Pi and the integrated repository source. It is a personal installation, not a project synchronization. The repository is still named <code>dragoscirjan/ai</code>; a planned rename is not an available source URL.</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">npx</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -y</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> skills@1.7.4</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> add</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> dragoscirjan/ai</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> \\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">  --skill</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> sync-my-skills</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --global</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --agent</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> pi</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --yes</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Expect exit code 0 and the canonical package under <code>~/.agents/skills/sync-my-skills</code>. For OpenCode or Claude Code, select <code>--agent opencode</code> or <code>--agent claude-code</code> instead. Review the <a href="https://github.com/dragoscirjan/ai/blob/main/.agents/skills/agentic-work/sync-my-skills/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">full manager guide</a> for the committed clean-export alternative and platform limits.</p><p>Install the package&#39;s pinned parser without lifecycle scripts:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">MANAGER</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">$HOME</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">/.agents/skills/sync-my-skills&quot;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">npm</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> ci</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --ignore-scripts</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --prefix</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">$MANAGER</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">node</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">$MANAGER</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">/scripts/sync-my-skills.mjs&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --help</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The help must include <code>inspect</code>, <code>prepare</code>, <code>review</code>, <code>review-instructions</code>, <code>plan</code>, <code>apply</code>, <code>status</code>, and <code>setup</code>. If the package or <code>yaml</code> import is missing, resolve that setup before project inspection. Do not install target-project dependencies merely to detect its needs.</p><h3 id="_2-plan-command-registration" tabindex="-1">2. Plan command registration <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-plan-command-registration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2. Plan command registration&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Run this read-only planning command from a trusted directory:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">node</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">$MANAGER</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">/scripts/sync-my-skills.mjs&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> setup</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --harnesses</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> pi</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Review <code>actions</code>, exact destinations, command content, and <code>planId</code>. Only after approving that plan, replace the placeholder below with its current identifier:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">node</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">$MANAGER</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">/scripts/sync-my-skills.mjs&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> setup</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --harnesses</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> pi</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> \\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">  --apply</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --confirm</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --plan-id</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> APPROVED_SETUP_PLAN_ID</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Expect <code>mode: setup-applied</code> and <code>reloadRequired: true</code>. Reload Pi with <code>/reload</code>. OpenCode and Claude Code use their own registration and reload behavior; select the corresponding <code>--harnesses</code> value and verify actual discovery. Existing conflicting commands are preserved, not overwritten to make setup pass.</p><h3 id="_3-inspect-a-project-and-choose-both-scopes" tabindex="-1">3. Inspect a project and choose both scopes <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-inspect-a-project-and-choose-both-scopes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3. Inspect a project and choose both scopes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Start the selected harness in the trusted target project and run its registered <code>sync-my-skills</code> entry point. In the Pi example:</p><div class="language-text vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">text</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span>/sync-my-skills</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The agent should inspect first, recommend a project-specific selection, and ask about every remaining active skill. It must assess optional instruction adoption separately. Declining either scope preserves its existing files; it does not override policy already active in the project.</p><p>Normal runs refresh and pin a compatible catalog snapshot. <code>--bundled</code> is an explicit offline or review choice, not a silent fallback or manager-code update.</p><h3 id="_4-review-the-exact-project-change" tabindex="-1">4. Review the exact project change <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-review-the-exact-project-change" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;4. Review the exact project change&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Before project mutation, approve the required isolated workspace. Review source acquisition, instruction requirements, semantic adaptations, legal files, target conflicts, and the final byte-bound plan. Approve only the exact current plan before apply.</p><p>A missing requirement stops the affected phase. A stale plan, modified file, unsupported catalog, or unresolved policy conflict requires a new review, not a bypass. New toolchains, websites, personal setup, deprecated removals, commits, and publication keep their own approval boundaries.</p><h3 id="_5-verify-the-installation-in-the-reported-workspace" tabindex="-1">5. Verify the installation in the reported workspace <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-verify-the-installation-in-the-reported-workspace" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5. Verify the installation in the reported workspace&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The manager&#39;s status should report the selected managed files as clean. Start the harness in that workspace and check its resource discovery and project-trust decision. Static files and symlinks are not proof of live model compliance.</p><p>Use the <a href="/projects/ai-skills/guide/first-use.html">first useful request</a> next. If the registered command or project skills are absent, check resource paths and reload behavior in the <a href="https://github.com/dragoscirjan/ai/blob/main/.agents/skills/agentic-work/sync-my-skills/README.md#recover-from-a-stopped-operation" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">manager recovery guide</a> before reinstalling or deleting anything.</p>`,36)])])}const g=s(n,[["render",l]]);export{k as __pageData,g as default};
